{"id":"mahabharata-3-092","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":92,"title":"द्विनवतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 92 · Lomasha on the fate of the wicked","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira wonders why he suffers while the unrighteous prosper. Lomasha answers that the wicked may flourish for a while, but like the arrogant demons of old they are soon destroyed, and so it will be with the Kauravas.","kn":"ಅಧರ್ಮಿಗಳು ಏಳಿಗೆ ಹೊಂದುತ್ತಿರುವಾಗ ತಾನೇಕೆ ನರಳುತ್ತಿದ್ದೇನೆ ಎಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಕೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದುಷ್ಟರು ಸ್ವಲ್ಪಕಾಲ ಬೆಳಗಬಹುದು, ಆದರೆ ಪ್ರಾಚೀನ ಗರ್ವಿತ ದೈತ್ಯರಂತೆ ಬೇಗ ನಾಶವಾಗುವರು, ಕೌರವರಿಗೂ ಹಾಗೆಯೇ ಆಗುವುದು ಎಂದು ಲೋಮಶರು ಉತ್ತರಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर सोचते हैं कि अधर्मी फलते-फूलते हैं तो वे क्यों दुःख पाते हैं। लोमश उत्तर देते हैं कि दुष्ट कुछ समय फल-फूल सकते हैं, पर प्राचीन अहंकारी दैत्यों की तरह शीघ्र नष्ट होते हैं, और कौरवों के साथ भी ऐसा ही होगा।","te":"అధర్మపరులు వర్ధిల్లుతుండగా తాను ఎందుకు కష్టపడుతున్నానని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు ప్రశ్నిస్తాడు. దుర్మార్గులు కొంతకాలం వర్ధిల్లవచ్చు, కానీ ప్రాచీన గర్విష్ఠ దైత్యుల వలె త్వరలోనే నశిస్తారు, కౌరవులకూ అలాగే జరుగుతుందని లోమశుడు బదులిస్తాడు.","ta":"அறமற்றோர் செழிக்கும்போது தாம் ஏன் துன்புறுகிறோம் என்று யுதிஷ்டிரர் வினவுகிறார். தீயோர் சிறிது காலம் செழிக்கலாம், ஆனால் பண்டைய செருக்கு மிக்க அசுரர்களைப் போல் விரைவில் அழிவர், கௌரவர்களுக்கும் அப்படியே நேரும் என்று லோமஶர் பதில் சொல்கிறார்.","ml":"അധർമ്മികൾ അഭിവൃദ്ധിപ്പെടുമ്പോൾ താൻ കഷ്ടപ്പെടുന്നതെന്തുകൊണ്ടെന്ന് യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ ചോദിക്കുന്നു. ദുഷ്ടന്മാർ കുറച്ചുകാലം തഴച്ചുവളർന്നേക്കാമെങ്കിലും പണ്ടത്തെ അഹങ്കാരികളായ അസുരന്മാരെപ്പോലെ അവർ വേഗം നശിക്കുമെന്ന് ലോമശൻ മറുപടി നൽകുന്നു; കൗരവരുടെ കാര്യത്തിലും അതുതന്നെ സംഭവിക്കുമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.92; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"तीर्थयात्रापर्व","titleEn":"Tirthayatra Parva (The pilgrimage)","verses":[{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"न वै निर्गुणमात्मानं मन्ये देवर्षिसत्तम ।\nतथास्मि दुःखसंतप्तो यथा नान्यो महीपतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of divine sages, I do not think myself without good qualities, yet I am tormented by grief as no other king is."}},{"n":2,"text":"परांश्च निर्गुणान्मन्ये न च धर्मरतानपि ।\nते च लोमश लोकेऽस्मिन्नृध्यन्ते केन केतुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"And I think my enemies lack good qualities and are not devoted to dharma, Lomasha. By what banner, then, do they prosper in this world?"}},{"text":"लोमश उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Lomasha said:"}},{"n":3,"text":"नात्र दुःखं त्वया राजन्कार्यं पार्थ कथंचन ।\nयदधर्मेण वर्धेरन्नधर्मरुचयो जनाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Pritha, you should never grieve, king, that people fond of adharma grow strong through adharma."}},{"n":4,"text":"वर्धत्यधर्मेण नरस्ततो भद्राणि पश्यति ।\nततः सपत्नाञ्जयति समूलस्तु विनश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man grows through adharma and sees good fortune, then conquers his rivals, but is destroyed in the end, root and all."}},{"n":5,"text":"मया हि दृष्टा दैतेया दानवाश्च महीपते ।\nवर्धमाना ह्यधर्मेण क्षयं चोपगताः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I have seen, lord of the earth, the Daityas and Danavas grow through adharma and then come to ruin again."}},{"n":6,"text":"पुरा देवयुगे चैव दृष्टं सर्वं मया विभो ।\nअरोचयन्सुरा धर्मं धर्मं तत्यजिरेऽसुराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago, in the age of the gods, I saw it all, lord: the gods loved dharma and the asuras abandoned dharma."}},{"n":7,"text":"तीर्थानि देवा विविशुर्नाविशन्भारतासुराः ।\nतानधर्मकृतो दर्पः पूर्वमेव समाविशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods entered the holy fords; the asuras, Bharata, did not. Pride had overtaken those doers of adharma from the first."}},{"n":8,"text":"दर्पान्मानः समभवन्मानात्क्रोधो व्यजायत ।\nक्रोधादह्रीस्ततोऽलज्जा वृत्तं तेषां ततोऽनशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"From pride came arrogance, from arrogance anger was born, from anger shamelessness, then lack of modesty, and their good conduct was lost."}},{"n":9,"text":"तानलज्जान्गतह्रीकान्हीनवृत्तान्वृथाव्रतान् ।\nक्षमा लक्ष्मीश्च धर्मश्च नचिरात्प्रजहुस्ततः ।\nलक्ष्मीस्तु देवानगमदलक्ष्मीरसुरान्नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those shameless, modesty-less, ill-conducted ones with empty vows were soon left by forbearance, prosperity and dharma. Prosperity went to the gods, king, and misfortune to the asuras."}},{"n":10,"text":"तानलक्ष्मीसमाविष्टान्दर्पोपहतचेतसः ।\nदैतेयान्दानवांश्चैव कलिरप्याविशत्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kali too entered those Daityas and Danavas, possessed by misfortune and their minds ruined by pride."}},{"n":11,"text":"तानलक्ष्मीसमाविष्टान्दानवान्कलिना तथा ।\nदर्पाभिभूतान्कौन्तेय क्रियाहीनानचेतसः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Kunti, the Danavas, possessed by misfortune and Kali, overcome by pride, without proper action and without sense, were soon overcome by arrogance and met destruction."}},{"n":12,"text":"मानाभिभूतानचिराद्विनाशः प्रत्यपद्यत ।\nनिर्यशस्यास्ततो दैत्याः कृत्स्नशो विलयं गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Soon the Daityas, deprived of glory, passed away entirely."}},{"n":13,"text":"देवास्तु सागरांश्चैव सरितश्च सरांसि च ।\nअभ्यगच्छन्धर्मशीलाः पुण्यान्यायतनानि च ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods, devoted to dharma, went to the oceans, rivers, lakes and holy shrines."}},{"n":14,"text":"तपोभिः क्रतुभिर्दानैराशीर्वादैश्च पाण्डव ।\nप्रजहुः सर्वपापानि श्रेयश्च प्रतिपेदिरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Pandava, by austerities, sacrifices, gifts and blessings they threw off all sins and attained the highest good."}},{"n":15,"text":"एवं हि दानवन्तश्च क्रियावन्तश्च सर्वशः ।\nतीर्थान्यगच्छन्विबुधास्तेनापुर्भूतिमुत्तमाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus the gods, rich in gifts and in rites everywhere, went to the fords and so gained supreme prosperity."}},{"n":16,"text":"तथा त्वमपि राजेन्द्र स्नात्वा तीर्थेषु सानुजः ।\nपुनर्वेत्स्यसि तां लक्ष्मीमेष पन्थाः सनातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So you too, king of kings, bathing at the fords with your brothers, will regain that fortune. This is the eternal way."}},{"n":17,"text":"यथैव हि नृगो राजा शिबिरौशीनरो यथा ।\nभगीरथो वसुमना गयः पूरुः पुरूरवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Just as King Nriga, Shibi son of Ushinara, Bhagiratha, Vasumanas, Gaya, Puru and Pururavas did,"}},{"n":18,"text":"चरमाणास्तपो नित्यं स्पर्शनादम्भसश्च ते ।\nतीर्थाभिगमनात्पूता दर्शनाच्च महात्मनाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"ever practising austerity, purified by the touch of water, by going to the fords and by seeing great souls,"}},{"n":19,"text":"अलभन्त यशः पुण्यं धनानि च विशां पते ।\nतथा त्वमपि राजेन्द्र लब्धासि विपुलां श्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"they won holy fame and wealth, lord of the people. So you too, king, will gain vast fortune."}},{"n":20,"text":"यथा चेक्ष्वाकुरचरत्सपुत्रजनबान्धवः ।\nमुचुकुन्दोऽथ मान्धाता मरुत्तश्च महीपतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Ikshvaku, with his sons, kinsmen and relatives, and Muchukunda, Mandhata and King Marutta did,"}},{"n":21,"text":"कीर्तिं पुण्यामविन्दन्त यथा देवास्तपोबलात् ।\nदेवर्षयश्च कार्त्स्न्येन तथा त्वमपि वेत्स्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"and as the gods and divine sages did by the power of austerity, and won holy fame, so will you also."}},{"n":22,"text":"धार्तराष्ट्रास्तु दर्पेण मोहेन च वशीकृताः ।\nनचिराद्विनशिष्यन्ति दैत्या इव न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"But the sons of Dhritarashtra, mastered by pride and delusion, will soon perish like the Daityas, without doubt."}}]}]}